      bearCase: "Both stocks may be entering overvalued territory after significant rallies. Microsoft faces intense competition in cloud and potential regulatory scrutiny. Starbucks is vulnerable to consumer discretionary spending fluctuations and execution risks in its global expansion. Broader market downturns or unforeseen macroeconomic shocks could negate positive momentum.",
      neutralCase: "While both companies have demonstrated strong performance and strategic execution, their stock prices already reflect much of this positive news. Future growth may be more incremental, and significant upside could be limited unless new, unforeseen catalysts emerge. Investors should expect a more moderate growth trajectory with continued market vigilance.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A moderately bullish outlook is warranted. The strong fundamentals and positive momentum are undeniable, but some of the recent gains may be priced in. Microsoft\'s strategic positioning in AI and cloud gives it a slight edge in long-term predictability. Starbucks\' turnaround is proving effective, but consumer sentiment can be more volatile. There\'s a higher probability of continued steady growth than a significant correction, but also less likelihood of another immediate large surge.",
